# Vercel uploads the working dir for CLI deploys; keep it to what the build needs.
# (GitHub deploys build from git and already exclude these via .gitignore.)
.git
node_modules
dist
.astro
.vercel
.claude
.firecrawl

# The Go pipeline is NOT part of the site. It is a parallel implementation of the
# raster/numeric work that runs offline on a workstation, and the site consumes only
# the committed artefacts in public/heat-map/data/ — which Python still produces.
# Nothing under src/ imports it, no WASM is shipped, and the build never invokes go.
# Excluded so CLI deploys stop uploading the source and its ~594 KB of parity
# fixtures to a build machine that has no use for either.
go
tests/fixtures/geo-oracle

# The 1024px logo master. It is the input to scripts/build-icons.mjs, and every
# icon it produces is generated ahead of time and committed, so the build never
# reads it — but sitting in public/ it would be uploaded AND served at 1.44 MB
# for nothing. Kept in the repo (regenerating icons needs it), kept off the CDN.
public/deltalogo.png

# Raw and oversized model sources are not used by the production build. Only
# the Draco-compressed public/models/river-1k.glb is requested at runtime.
models-src
public/models/._river-1k.glb
public/models/river-2k.glb
public/models/river-8k.glb
public/models/river-4k.glb
public/models/._nature_vegetation_pack.glb
public/models/flora.glb
public/models/flora_raw.glb
public/models/flowers_pack_4.glb
public/models/nature_vegetation_pack.glb

# Research, design history, and local-only scratch. NOTE: scripts/ must NOT be
# ignored here — the build command runs node scripts/prune-dist-assets.mjs, and
# CLI deploys upload the working dir, so excluding it breaks the remote build.
attic
docs
inspiration
previews
Delta_Climate_Research_Speedrun_Guide.pdf
Delta_Climate_Research_Visual_Layout_Guide.pdf
